   "summary": "Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2021 updated title 39’s franked-mail rules in section 3210. It changed the name of the House body to “House Communications Standards Commission,” removed one category from section 3210(a)(3), revised the text in section 3210(a)(3)(I), and added a clause allowing certain personal matter to a constituent [2020-116-260-3210-2] [2020-116-260-3210-3] [2020-116-260-3210-4] [2020-116-260-3210-7] [2020-116-260-3210-8].\n\nThe law also changed timing and formatting rules in section 3210 by removing the House-specific 90-day language, changing one 90-day reference to 60 days, and adding a new clause in section 3210(a)(6)(E). It also made conforming name changes in sections 3216 and 3220 [2020-116-260-3210-9] [2020-116-260-3210-10] [2020-116-260-3210-13] [2020-116-260-3216-1] [2020-116-260-3220-1]",
   "summary_key": "4fd57a4cd15cfbae3e10176d7b3c267cfe548724776677e67c0cb3bb4d214c4a",
