   "summary": "Postal Service Reform Act of 2022 amended title 39 to require an integrated Postal Service network with delivery at least six days a week, and it changed the general postal policy language to require service that is prompt, economical, consistent, and reliable, with operational efficiency and reduced complexity [2022-117-108-101-1] [2022-117-108-101-2] [2022-117-108-101-3] [2022-117-108-101-4] [2022-117-108-101-5]. It also changed Postal Regulatory Commission governance and funding rules, including joint appointment of the Commission’s chief officer, a new budget process for the Commission, and the removal of a former subsection in section 504 [2022-117-108-202-1] [2022-117-108-202-2] [2022-117-108-504-1] [2022-117-108-504-2] [2022-117-108-2003-1] [2022-117-108-2009-1] [2022-117-108-2009-2]. The Act added chapter 37 provisions authorizing nonpostal products and services, definitions, intergovernmental agreements, programs for other agencies, annual reporting, and performance targets, and it also added section 2903 on sale proceeds after permanent cessation of operations [2022-117-108-3701-1] [2022-117-108-3702-1] [2022-117-108-3703-1] [2022-117-108-3704-1] [2022-117-108-3705-1] [2022-117-108-3692-1] [2022-117-108-2903-1].",
